+## Subtopics
+
+### [Hexahedron Projection for Curvilinear Grids](1111-hexahedron-projection-for-curvilinear-grids.md)
+A method to classify projections of hexahedra from curvilinear meshes into triangle fans or strips for hardware rendering, avoiding the computational geometry complexity of general line-sweep subdivision by handling specific topological cases.
+
+### [Per-vertex edge classification for view-independent cell projection](1503-per-vertex-edge-classification-for-view-independent-cell-pro.md)
+A technique to avoid defects in per-vertex classification during rasterization by ensuring at least one vertex on an edge has the correct classification of the second face sharing the edge, affecting the whole edge during rasterization.
 
 ## Operating characteristics
-- **Time Complexity:** Sorting is O(n) for MPVO [S3, unofficial]. Subdivision is view-dependent and may increase polygon count [S3, unofficial]. Detection of problem cells requires plane equation tests [S3, unofficial].
+- **Time Complexity:** Sorting is O(n) for MPVO [S3, unofficial]. Subdivision is view-dependent and may increase polygon count [S3, unofficial]. Detection of problem cells requires plane equation tests [S1].
 - **Memory Complexity:** Increased memory usage for storing subdivided cells and tetrahedra. Data structures must track subdivision state [S3, unofficial].
 - **Measured Performance:** On a half-cylindrical shell with 19,000 cells, the method handles non-planar faces effectively [S3, unofficial]. Subdividing all quadrilaterals increases polygon count significantly but maintains fragment count [S3, unofficial].
 - **Scaling:** Scales with the number of cells and the complexity of the grid topology. View-dependent subdivision adds overhead per frame [S3, unofficial].
-- **Strengths:** Works directly on general grid topology without resampling. Handles non-planar faces and visibility cycles. Compatible with standard graphics hardware [S1][S3, unofficial].
-- **Limitations:** Approximations in perspective views (linear interpolation of $\tau$ and color). Inconsistent with analytic integration unless strict conditions are met. Increased polygon count if all quadrilaterals are subdivided [S2, book][S3, unofficial].
